# Website Exploration for Testing

Explores a running website using browser automation to identify key functionalities and generate test cases.

## When to Apply

- User asks to explore a website for testing
- Need to identify core features and user flows
- Want to generate test cases from a live site

## Instructions

1. Navigate to the provided URL using Chrome DevTools MCP. If no URL is provided, ask the user.
2. Identify and interact with 3-5 core features or user flows.
3. Document user interactions, relevant UI elements (and their locators), and expected outcomes.
4. Close the browser context upon completion.
5. Provide a concise summary of findings.
6. Propose and generate test cases based on the exploration.
